The harness loads MEMORY.md through one function: trim, keep 200 lines,
cut at the last newline at or before UTF-16 unit 25,000, append a WARNING.
Read from the installed claude 2.1.261 binary and confirmed end to end
with two synthetic indexes through the real harness (135 of 180 lines at
33,119 units; 200 of 220 at the line cap). The live index was 25,201
units and its newest entry was past the cut for every new session.

scripts/memory_index_drift.py now replicates the cut exactly, reports
OVER_CAP / OVER_BUDGET / MISPLACED / DUPLICATE / MISSING_TARGET /
GROUP_COUNT_STALE on a second dashboard line, reads pointer lines from
MEMORY.md and every _index_<group>.md so a demoted file is still judged
on both halves of its summary, skips tier-2 files as memories, reminds
the editor of an index file at the moment of the write, and gains
--demote, which moves a pointer line verbatim to its group file and
never deletes. main() reads every line for its exit code.

Rejected: shortening other people's lines (a delay, and the 200-line cap
still arrives); merging entries by judgment (buries facts). The split is
the only shape without a ceiling.

